<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RSW_ExtremeDesertSignatureFlora.xml         EXTREME_DESERT_SIGNATURE_FLORA_1

  Authors the Extreme Desert's own named signature flora, in place of the
  single unverified donor plant (RSW_Plant_Bloddle) that was carrying the
  whole 3,969-tile biome alone. Two design sheets, both FROZEN
  (BIOME_FREEZE_FABLE_REVIEW_1):

    dune_sea.md    SS4  "glass-nub light-pipes" — the only visible part of
                        almost everything alive on the deep dayside; the
                        actual photosynthetic biology is 1-3m underground.
                   SS7  "Optical-grade biosilica" — the light-pipe nubs are
                        real lenses.
    deep_desert.md SS4b "the ollim, the tree that grows to cast shade" —
                        an inverted plant, no leaves, non-photosynthetic,
                        bone-white, geological growth rate. Final name
                        **ollim** (owner ruling 2026-09-20, this item;
                        supersedes the working names "Silverpan"/
                        "Silverbole"). "Silverbole" survives only as
                        descriptive prose for the look, never as a name.

  Three ThingDefs, not two: the two FLORA defs the item names
  (RSW_LightPipeNub, RSW_Ollim) plus RSW_OllimWood, the harvested wood
  material deep_desert.md SS4b actually specifies the signature on
  ("Silverbole wood is a material with a unique stat signature") — same
  relationship as RSW_Plant_Bloddle -> RSW_RawBloddle in
  RSW_DesertPortB_Plants.xml, one door down. The "silver required" ask
  (deep_desert.md's Owed note) is satisfied here by the MATERIAL, not the
  name: RSW_OllimWood is bone-white/silvery in colour and carries the
  heat-immune / sharp-and-blunt-weak stat signature the sheet describes,
  even though the coined name (check_pseudo_sw_name.py, PASS) does not
  itself contain "silver".

  Stats read from vanilla WoodLog via mcp__rimsage__get_def_details
  2026-09-20 (Flammability 1, StuffPower_Armor_Sharp/Blunt 0.54,
  StuffPower_Armor_Heat 0.4, StuffPower_Insulation_Heat 4) and deliberately
  inverted on the heat axis, weakened on the sharp/blunt axis, per
  deep_desert.md SS4b's own words: "near-total immunity to heat and flame
  damage... and correspondingly helpless against sharp and blunt."

  Art: no existing render found for ollim/silverbole/light-pipe/glass-nub
  in infrastructure/artpipe/{done,_artsrc,registry.jsonl} (checked
  2026-09-20 per CLAUDE.md's "Check for existing regenerated art before
  queuing more"). Three jobs filed 2026-09-20 (rslpn_v1, rswollim_v1,
  rswollimwood_v1); all three RENDERED (facts PASS, real alpha, correct
  canvas — infrastructure/artpipe/done/*.manifest.json) and deployed
  2026-09-24 to their real texPaths below, replacing the WoodLog
  placeholder on the wood resource.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ============== Light-pipe nub — the dune sea's whole visible biome ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RSW_LightPipeNub</defName>
    <label>light-pipe nub</label>
    <description>A knuckle of water-clear, silica-cemented glass, flush with the sand and easy to miss until it catches the light. It is not a leaf and it has never been one — it is a lens, the only part of this organism that has ever seen the sun. Everything that actually does the plant's living is a metre or more underground, cool and out of sight, fed by whatever light this nub admits and nothing else. Walk the dune sea and you are walking over almost all of it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Nutrition>0</Nutrition>
      <Beauty>1</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- rslpn_v1 rendered + deployed 2026-09-24 (256x256, real alpha, facts PASS). -->
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RSW_LightPipeNub</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>2</pathCost>
    <!-- MEASURED live 2026-09-21: `Config error in RSW_LightPipeNub: Nutrition == 0 but
         preferability is RawBad instead of NeverForNutrition`. A lens of silica-cemented
         glass is deliberately Nutrition 0, so the inherited preferability is what is wrong.
         ⚠️ This was a bare `<ingestible />` and reparenting to PlantBaseNonEdible did NOT
         fix it — MEASURED on the same day, it made it worse: an empty element does not
         suppress the field, it constructs a bare IngestibleProperties, so with no parent
         ingestible to merge into the load then reported `undefined preferability` AND
         `no foodType`. Name the one field that is wrong and inherit the rest. -->
    <ingestible>
      <preferability>NeverForNutrition</preferability>
    </ingestible>
    <plant>
      <!-- Item-specified: fertilityMin 0.05. Tiny and glassy: near-zero footprint,
           no wind exposure (it does not stand proud of the sand), no leaves to lose. -->
      <fertilityMin>0.05</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>10</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <maxMeshCount>4</maxMeshCount>
      <visualSizeRange>0.12~0.20</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0</topWindExposure>
      <wildClusterRadius>1</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>2</wildClusterWeight>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <wildEqualLocalDistribution>true</wildEqualLocalDistribution>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ============== Ollim — the tree that grows to cast shade ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="TreeBase">
    <defName>RSW_Ollim</defName>
    <label>ollim</label>
    <description>A bone-white shield rising out of the sand on a flat-topped trunk, standing where the faintest hint of buried moisture fed the growth of a single cell — centuries ago, and again, and again. It is photosynthetic in nothing and grows no leaf; its entire purpose above ground is casting the one patch of permanent shade for kilometres, over the seep or the corpse or the buried water that might one day sustain it. A stand of them is older than any ruin, and the true bones of vast dead things are usually growing up through the sand around their feet.</description>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <ThingDef>RSW_OllimWood</ThingDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
    <fillPercent>0.35</fillPercent>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- rswollim_v1 rendered + deployed 2026-09-24 (1024x1024, real alpha, facts PASS). -->
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RSW_Ollim</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <!-- No fire ecology in this biome (dune_sea.md/deep_desert.md hard ban) and the
           tree itself is the fireproof half of the "heat-immune / sharp-weak" signature -
           see RSW_OllimWood below for the harvested material's own stats. -->
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <MaxHitPoints>350</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>220</Mass>
      <Nutrition>0</Nutrition>
      <Beauty>4</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>6</BeautyOutdoors>
    </statBases>
    <!-- MEASURED live 2026-09-21: `Config error in RSW_Ollim: Nutrition == 0 but
         preferability is RawBad instead of NeverForNutrition`. "It is photosynthetic in
         nothing and grows no leaf" — Nutrition 0 is deliberate. Core's TreeBase parents off
         PlantBase, which carries `<ingestible>` with preferability RawBad, and there is no
         non-edible tree base to switch to (unlike RSW_LightPipeNub above, which could just
         use PlantBaseNonEdible), so the preferability is overridden here instead.
         foodType is left inherited: only preferability is wrong. -->
    <ingestible>
      <preferability>NeverForNutrition</preferability>
    </ingestible>
    <plant>
      <!-- "Accretes cell by cell from the tiniest hint of moisture, over spans that
           make its growth effectively geological" (deep_desert.md SS4b): near-zero
           fertility requirement, fertility-insensitive growth rate, immortal once
           grown (lifespanDaysPerGrowDays 0, as RUT_PaleTree — another single sacred
           landmark tree in this repo), and no leaves to ever lose. -->
      <fertilityMin>0.03</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>400</growDays>
      <lifespanDaysPerGrowDays>0</lifespanDaysPerGrowDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <dieIfNoSunlight>False</dieIfNoSunlight>
      <dieFromToxicFallout>False</dieFromToxicFallout>
      <visualSizeRange>3.5~5.5</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0.15</topWindExposure>
      <treeCategory>Super</treeCategory>
      <harvestedThingDef>RSW_OllimWood</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>15</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>700</harvestWork>
      <harvestTag>Wood</harvestTag>
      <harvestMinGrowth>0.5</harvestMinGrowth>
      <harvestFailable>false</harvestFailable>
      <treeLoversCareIfChopped>true</treeLoversCareIfChopped>
      <allowAutoCut>false</allowAutoCut>
      <warnIfMarkedForCut>true</warnIfMarkedForCut>
      <!-- Solitary, not clustered: "a silverbole is a small ecosystem standing
           alone in open ground" (deep_desert.md SS4b) — small radius, small
           weight, so wild spawns come up alone rather than in a grove. Overall
           rarity is governed by RUT_ExtremeDesert's wildPlants commonality
           (0.01), not by these fields. -->
      <wildClusterRadius>2</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>2</wildClusterWeight>
      <wildOrder>3</wildOrder>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ============== Ollim wood — the "silver required" material signature ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RSW_OllimWood</defName>
    <label>ollim wood</label>
    <description>Wood struck from an ollim stand — bone-white, dense as stone, and grown so slowly that a single plank predates most ruins on the planet. It shrugs off fire and blistering heat the way almost nothing else does, but a hard strike shatters it clean through: the tree traded strength for the one thing that actually kept it alive out here. Prized in a handful of recipes for exactly that trade-off.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- rswollimwood_v1 rendered + deployed 2026-09-24 (256x256, real alpha, facts
           PASS), replacing the vanilla-WoodLog placeholder. -->
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RSW_OllimWood</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Wood_Drop</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Wood_Drop</soundDrop>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Light</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <burnableByRecipe>true</burnableByRecipe>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>7</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.5</Mass>
      <MaxHitPoints>150</MaxHitPoints>
      <DeteriorationRate>0.3</DeteriorationRate>
      <!-- Heat-immune / sharp-and-blunt-weak signature (deep_desert.md SS4b), calibrated
           against measured vanilla WoodLog (Flammability 1, StuffPower_Armor_Sharp/Blunt
           0.54, StuffPower_Armor_Heat 0.4, StuffPower_Insulation_Heat 4,
           SharpDamageMultiplier 0.4, BluntDamageMultiplier 0.9 — mcp__rimsage__get_def_details,
           2026-09-20): heat/flame axis inverted to near-immune, sharp/blunt axis inverted
           to fragile. -->
      <Flammability>0.03</Flammability>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Sharp>0.15</StuffPower_Armor_Sharp>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Blunt>0.15</StuffPower_Armor_Blunt>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Heat>1.8</StuffPower_Armor_Heat>
      <StuffPower_Insulation_Cold>6</StuffPower_Insulation_Cold>
      <StuffPower_Insulation_Heat>30</StuffPower_Insulation_Heat>
      <SharpDamageMultiplier>1.6</SharpDamageMultiplier>
      <BluntDamageMultiplier>1.6</BluntDamageMultiplier>
    </statBases>
    <stuffProps>
      <stuffAdjective>ollim</stuffAdjective>
      <categories>
        <li>Woody</li>
      </categories>
      <appearance>Planks</appearance>
      <commonality>0.015</commonality>
      <!-- Bone-white/silvery — this is the "silver required" ask (deep_desert.md Owed
           note), satisfied by the material's colour and stats rather than by the name. -->
      <color>(232,227,214)</color>
      <constructEffect>ConstructWood</constructEffect>
      <soundImpactBullet>BulletImpact_Wood</soundImpactBullet>
      <soundMeleeHitSharp>MeleeHit_Wood</soundMeleeHitSharp>
      <soundMeleeHitBlunt>MeleeHit_Wood</soundMeleeHitBlunt>
      <soundImpactMelee>Pawn_Melee_Punch_HitBuilding_Wood</soundImpactMelee>
      <statFactors>
        <MaxHitPoints>0.55</MaxHitPoints>
        <Beauty>1.5</Beauty>
        <Flammability>0.05</Flammability>
        <WorkToMake>1.1</WorkToMake>
        <WorkToBuild>1.1</WorkToBuild>
      </statFactors>
      <canSuggestUseDefaultStuff>true</canSuggestUseDefaultStuff>
    </stuffProps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
